  "description": "Poseidon X Origin\n\nSerious Gravel Riding. An Open Invitation.\n\nThe road that turns to dirt. The climb you’ve been meaning to try. The feeling that there’s more out there—and you’re ready for it.\n\nThe X Origin is our way of making serious gravel riding more accessible. Our proven X family frame, an all-new full-carbon fork, and thoughtfully selected components create a capable foundation for your first gravel event, everyday escapes, and ambitions that grow with every ride.\n\nHead out early. Take the unfamiliar turn. See where it leads.\n\nA Proven Foundation.\n\nThe tried-and-tested Poseidon X family frame combines double-butted, heat-treated 6061 aluminum alloy with our Ambition Geometry.\n\nAn approachable riding position and mixed-surface versatility make it a natural companion for weekday miles and the longer way home.\n\nA More Forgiving Fork. A Familiar Feature Returns.\n\nThe all-new full-carbon fork features a layup designed with a more forgiving ride in mind, bringing a comfort-focused approach to weathered pavement and winding gravel roads.\n\nAnd fork mounting points are back. You asked for the versatility you loved on the older X. We listened. Mount compatible accessories and make room for the ride you have in mind.\n\nSettle In with ROAM.\n\nDebuting on the X Origin, the Poseidon ROAM Saddle brings a shorter, wider, ergonomically tested shape informed by rider feedback. Higher-quality supportive foam, a comfortable and durable synthetic leather cover, and refined finishing make it ready for everyday miles and longer adventures.\n\nFind Your Gear. Follow the Road.\n\nMicroSHIFT Sword Black shifters pair with an ADVENT 9-speed rear derailleur for reliable, straightforward shifting.\n\nA 38T steel chainring and 11–46T cassette deliver a broad gearing range, including a below-one-to-one climbing gear. A through-spindle crankset and external-cup bottom bracket round out the drivetrain.\n\nFind your cadence. Keep exploring.\n\nMeet the Pro5 performance brake calipers\n\nPoseidon Pro5 mechanical-hydraulic performance brake calipers pair with compressionless brake housing for a firm, responsive lever feel and controlled braking.\n\nCable actuation meets hydraulic operation at the caliper—a thoughtful combination for everyday miles and gravel adventures.\n\nReady for the Detour.\n\nKenda Happy Medium 700×40C tires bring versatility to rides that connect pavement, hard-packed dirt, and gravel.\n\nThe Origin’s traditional hooked clincher wheels use an established hub design with durability and everyday capability at their core. Front and rear thru-axles provide secure wheel attachment, modern standards, and flexibility for compatible wheel upgrades as your riding evolves.\n\nThese wheels use inner tubes and are not tubeless-compatible.\n\nThe Details.\n\nFork: All-new full carbon with accessory mounting points.\n\nDrivetrain: MicroSHIFT Sword Black shifters with an ADVENT 9-speed rear derailleur.\n\nCrankset: Through-spindle design with an external-cup bottom bracket.\n\nBrakes: Poseidon iPro 5.0 mechanical-hydraulic performance brake calipers with compressionless housing.\n\nYour Next Chapter Starts Outside.\n\nThe early starts. The earned views. The road you’ve passed a hundred times becoming a place you finally know.\n\nThe X Origin opens the door to serious gravel riding. Bring your curiosity—and see how far it takes you.\n\nFIND YOUR NOW.",
